Pre-Depends: dpkg (>= 1.16.1)
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, rpi-make-boot-image, sed (>= 4.9), bash (>= 5.2), debian-archive-keyring, raspberrypi-archive-keyring, fakeroot, rpi-modcopy, rsync, systemd, kmod, cpio, zstd, dpkg-dev
Recommends: curl, wget, dctrl-tools, coreutils (>= 9.1), gzip (>= 1.12), zstd (>= 1.5.4), mtools, init-system-helpers
Suggests: mmdebstrap, uidmap, gnupg, qemu-user-static, binfmt-support
Description: Tool to create cut-down Debian-based OS-images for Raspberry Pi Devices
 pi-gen-micro is a lightweight tool for creating minimal Debian-based
 operating system images optimized for Raspberry Pi devices. It allows
 for customization of the base system while maintaining a small footprint,
 making it ideal for embedded systems and IoT applications that require
 a compact, efficient OS with the reliability of Debian, and the enhanced
 features of Raspberry Pi OS.
 .
 This package includes utilities and scripts necessary for building
 custom Raspberry Pi OS images with reduced size and resource requirements.
 .
 pi-gen-micro-sysroot(1) additionally allows images to be built on hosts that
 are not running Raspberry Pi OS, and without root, by bootstrapping a Debian
 build sysroot with mmdebstrap and entering it via a user namespace. That path
 needs mmdebstrap, uidmap and gnupg; building for a foreign architecture also
 needs qemu-user-static and binfmt-support.
